ush-disabled, async-delivery-unobservable, remote-not-found, invalid-destination), justified by avoiding a permanent 'pending' alarm for supported local-only stores. But no acceptance criterion asserts the negative case: that a local-only / push-disabled store does NOT produce a spurious pending marker. Without that test the very alarm-fatigue regression the split exists to prevent can silently reappear.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa264f0544eef35d8","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"D4 'NOT recorded' and Acceptance criteria","norm_id":"n1319924d88557ca0","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["A local-only store (sync.push disabled) — a supported mode — regresses so push_status() latches 'pending' forever, and no test catches it."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add AC8: with sync.push disabled (and separately with remote-not-found), a write leaves NO pending marker and push_status() returns state == 'ok' — asserted by a test.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the marker's concurrency contract: atomic write (write-temp-then-rename) and the ordering/last-writer rule between the detached async child's record and a foreground clear.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T6","T7","T9"],"criteria":["T9","T5b"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.4475,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'push.py re-spawns the push as a detached Popen(..., start_new_session=True), never waited'","D3: 'the default path (and the detached child, same function) records while still returning None' and 'A successful push clears the marker'","ABSENCE: no statement of how a clear from a foreground push and a record from the still-running detached child are serialized against each other"],"finding":"The durable marker is shared mutable state written from concurrent processes (the detached async push child and a subsequent foreground write/clear), but the plan does not specify atomic write / last-writer-wins / TOCTOU handling for the marker file.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f20241ca0e5d11834","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"D2 marker location / D3 record-and-clear","norm_id":"n3619ecdcda0218b9","priority":0.5025,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["A detached async push is still running (about to record a failure) when a subsequent foreground write succeeds and clears the marker — order determines whether status latches wrong","Two writers race on the same marker path producing a partial/torn file"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"State that record_failure/clear write via a temp file + atomic rename in the git dir, and define the reconciliation rule (e.g. clear only stamps ok with a monotonic since/epoch so a late child record cannot resurrect a cleared marker).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Specify WHERE the marker clear is invoked for every successful-push return in push.py (first-attempt success, post-recovery terminal success), since the clear has no single choke point the way recording does.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.2975,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["D3: 'A successful push clears the marker.'","push.py success returns are not funnelled: line 577 `if terminal.returncode == 0: return`, plus the normal-path success return in the retry loop — no clear-choke-point analogous to _raise_if_strict","AC4 asserts the observable outcome but the design does not pin the clear insertion points"],"finding":"D3 gives recording a single choke point (`_raise_if_strict`) so 'no call site changes, no path missed', but the symmetric CLEAR ('a successful push clears the marker') has no equivalent single choke point — successful-push returns are scattered bare `return`s (push.py:577 terminal-after-recovery, and the in-loop success return), and the plan neither enumerates them nor states where the clear is invoked.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f18efde1c893bbc9e","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Design D3; AC4","norm_id":"n8d6ddd2e8b549d7f","priority":0.5025,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["A push that succeeds on the first attempt vs. after non-fast-forward recovery take different return paths; a clear placed on only one leaves a latched-pending marker after a real success"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"State the concurrency discipline for the shared marker (e.g. atomic write, or record only under a lock / with monotonic ordering) so a concurrent record and clear from two writers on the same tracker cannot produce a stale state.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.2975,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["D1: 'Best-effort: every entry point swallows its own errors' addresses I/O failure, not concurrent record-vs-clear ordering","push.py:738 push_after_commit and the async detached child (push.py:466) and the reconciler all invoke push_tickets_branch on the canonical tracker","D3 records under the write lock's push? No — push_tickets_branch runs OUTSIDE the write lock (push_after_commit note: 'Call AFTER the locked commit has released the store lock')"],"finding":"The marker is a single file in the tracker git dir, but multiple processes push the SAME tracker concurrently (detached async child, reconciler subprocess, and inline `push_after_commit` writers), so a concurrent record (failing writer) and clear (succeeding writer) on one shared marker is last-writer-wins with no stated ordering/atomicity discipline.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f31e5810eac0dedc7","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Design D1/D2/D3 (push_state record/clear)","norm_id":"n7260b2bdef265376","priority":0.5025,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["Writer A's push fails and records `pending`; concurrently writer B's push succeeds and clears — the clear may land after A's record and mask a genuine outage, or A's record may land after B's clear and re-latch a stale failure"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_e